As will be seen later, this transformation allows good evaluation of the results of Principal Component Analysis at the level of exploratory data analysis, signiﬁcantly reducing bias that might otherwise occur. These results allow to address important aspects with respect to the behaviour of the elements and to support additional inferences con cerning palaeoenvironmental or diagenetic conditions associated with the samples.
